# Files tracked in ~/dotfiles that are deliberately NOT dotter-mapped.
# Read by `dotter-drift-monitor --orphans` (alias `dotter-orphan-detector-v2`).
#
# Every rule must cite one of the four exclusion criteria from
# DOTTER-CROSS-PLATFORM-MASTER-GUIDE.md § "What belongs in dotter":
#   1 secrets   2 per-machine data   3 outside $HOME / needs sudo   4 compiled or generated
# or be repo plumbing / documentation. Anything not mapped and not matched here
# is reported as an orphan and the check exits 1. Syntax is gitignore-flavoured:
# no `/` = basename anywhere; trailing `/` = that directory and below;
# `**` crosses directories, `*` does not; leading `/` anchors to the repo root.

# --- repo plumbing and documentation (not deployable files) ---
.gitignore
.stignore
.github/
.dotter/
*.md
docs/
git-hooks/                 # installed into .git/hooks by git-hooks/setup-hooks, not into $HOME
.DS_Store

# --- 4: sources that are built, not deployed as files ---
rust-projects/             # deployed as binaries in ~/.local/bin (rust-redeploy)
browser-extensions/        # built into signed .xpi files and installed via AMO
__pycache__/
**/cache/
**/logs/

# --- 4: generated — state-capture baselines written nightly to the repo root ---
/*.txt

# --- 3: outside $HOME, installed with sudo per gmpull.md / NIMBINI-LOG-ROTATION.md ---
etc/

# --- retired components kept for history (do not deploy) ---
legacy/
